<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Wit Nigel buys JCI option.</title>
<headline>Wit Nigel buys JCI option.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Witwatersrand Nigel Ltd said on Tuesday it would acquire an option to buy up to 7.41 million shares in JCI Ltd at 54.50 rand each for 22.24 million rand. The option is exercisable before April 2, 1998.</p>
<p>Wit Nigel will also acquire 10 million shares in Saflife Ltd, which owns 30 percent of JCI, for 20.00 rand each.</p>
<p>As a result of the transactions, the African Mining Group consortium, which recently acquired conttrol of JCI, will have a 67.2 percent holding in Wit Nigel.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
